From ae236ee077ace7779ff577ff2297b77ff8d2a05c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: purplewall1206 <purplewall1206@github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 07:21:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: CortenMM arena: debugfs observability (arenas ledger,
 arena_stats)

S8 (M3b): pure-observability slice, debugfs + shell + KUnit only, zero
hot-path changes.

- Global arena ledger: every live arena of every mm registered via
  list_add_rcu() as the last DECLARE publishing step (after all failure
  paths, so no half-registered entry), unlinked with list_del_rcu() at
  RELEASE/mm_exit after the arena is gone from its registry (RELEASE
  erases the per-mm xarray frames first); the descriptor is freed with
  kfree_rcu() on a dedicated rcu_head, so RCU readers never touch freed
  memory.  debugfs cannot enumerate mm_structs, hence this second,
  purely observational bookkeeping -- the per-mm xarrays remain the
  source of truth and the fault path never touches the list.
- debugfs "arenas" file: one line per live arena (mm, cached shadow-VMA,
  range, prot, active/dying), walked under rcu_read_lock() with no new
  lock contention: readers take neither ctl_lock nor the ledger
  spinlock, and writers touch the ledger only on cold paths.
- debugfs "arena_stats" file: the protocol-layer lines (corten_stats_
  lines(), factored out of corten_stats_show so both files share one
  source, no drift) plus the arena aggregate: live arena count and a
  global drain_timeout mirror of the per-mm CORTEN_ARENA_STAT_DRAIN_
  TIMEOUTS counters, which are not reachable from debugfs (r03
  final-smoke legacy item 1).
- KUnit: obs-ledger declare/RELEASE visibility and the drain-timeout
  aggregate wiring (injected; a real timeout requires a kernel bug).

Fold-in review (night-end compression, by maintainer):
- RCU discipline: registration after all DECLARE failure paths, so no
  half-registered entry; deregistration after the arena left its
  registry; kfree_rcu() pairing with the RCU ledger walk is correct.
- Read side: rcu_read_lock() walk only, no ctl_lock/ledger lock/mmap
  lock -- no new contention anywhere.
- Rendering: arena_stats reuses the factored-out protocol lines; two
  comment inaccuracies fixed (ctl_lock claim did not cover the mm_exit
  unlink; "dying" is effectively unobservable since RELEASE
  deregisters before the drain kill).

Verification: KUnit off 25+10+3 / on 24+11+13 all green; guest arena
ledger live-checked (declare shows the range active, RELEASE removes
it); checkpatch.pl 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 checks.

Signed-off-by: purplewall1206 <purplewall1206@github.com>
